There are two things not included with this archive to be able to run the BBS. The
file transfers require an XPR driver called XPRD. Since this driver was not written
by me, I can not include it with my BBS. The file XPRD105.LHA is available for you
to download from library #3 on my BBS though. The other file not included is the
sound program which plays an IFF sound. This is used when a user pages you for a
chat. Once again, since I did not write the sound program, I can not include it in
the archive for the BBS. The file SOUND.LHA is available for you to download from
library #5 on my BBS though. If you have some other sound player then you may be
able to use that instead. Just make sure you have the sound player in your c dir
and that it is called SOUND. The BBS will work without the sound program just fine
but you will not be able to have an IFF sound played to page you for a chat. The
BBS will work without the XPRD program as long as you do not wish to have users
upload or download anything.

                                         Lawrence McClafferty
